Description: zink: check 3D image support in is_format_supported
 zink_is_format_supported() only queries the image format properties when a
 sample count is given. For sample count 0, which the state tracker uses when
 it picks texture formats, it answers from the format features alone. These
 do not say whether a 3D image of the format can be created: pvr reports
 sampled-image support for the ASTC and ETC2 formats with optimal tiling but
 rejects VK_IMAGE_TYPE_3D for every block-compressed format
 (pvr_get_image_format_properties()). zink then claimed 3D ASTC textures and
 failed later in resource creation, when check_ici() found no image config.
 .
 For PIPE_TEXTURE_3D query the image format properties as for one sample;
 3D images are single-sampled. Other targets are unchanged.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
